b-id pub-id-type="pmid">15138258</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Shintani, T., W.-P. Huang, P.E. Stromhaug, and D.J. Klionsky. <year>2002</year>. Mechanism of cargo selection in the cytoplasm to vacuole targeting pathway. <source>Dev. Cell.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>825</fpage>&#x02013;837.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12479808</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Tucker, K.A., F. Reggiori, W.A. Dunn Jr., and D.J. Klionsky. <year>2003</year>. Atg23 is essential for the cytoplasm to vacuole targeting pathway and efficient autophagy but not pexophagy. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>278</volume>:<fpage>48445</fpage>&#x02013;48452.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14504273</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Wang, C.-W., J. Kim, W.-P. Huang, H. Abeliovich, P.E. Stromhaug, W.A. Dunn Jr., and D.J. Klionsky. <year>2001</year>. Apg2 is a novel protein required for the cytoplasm to vacuole targeting, autophagy, and pexophagy pathways. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>30442</fpage>&#x02013;30451.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11382760</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="other">Yen, W.-L., J.E. Legakis, U. Nair, and D.J. Klionsky. <year>2006</year>. Atg27 is required for autophagy-dependent cycling of Atg9. <italic>Mol. Biol. Cell.</italic> In press.</citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Yorimitsu, T., and D.J. Klionsky. <year>2005</year>. Atg11 links cargo to the vesicle-forming machinery in the cytoplasm to vacuole targeting pathway. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>1593</fpage>&#x02013;1605.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15659643</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><citation citation-type="journal">Young, A.R.J., E.Y.W. Chan, X.W. Hu, R. K&#x000f6;chl, S.G. Crawshaw, S. High, D.W. Hailey, J. Lippincott-Schwartz, and S.A. Tooze. <year>2006</